// Victor Lang's guaranty of Dana Cole's loan from Ines Marlow (guaranty.md).
Document "guaranty.md"

Fact lender Identified by Ines
Fact borrower Identified by Dana
Fact guarantor Identified by Victor
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Param loan : Money(USD, 2) = 800000
Param limit : Money(USD, 2) = 500000
Param term : Duration = 90
Param notice-window : Duration = 30

// 1.1 The loan, and default on it
Var balance Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Duty repay Holder borrower Claimant lender
  Holds when balance > 0
  Due within term
Act pay-loan Actor borrower Recipient lender Related to usd
  Holds when usd <= balance
  Creates balance(balance - usd)
Bool in-default Holds when Violated(repay())

// 3. Notice of default, within thirty days
Bool notified
Duty notice-due Holder lender Claimant guarantor
  Holds when in-default() && Not(notified())
  Violated when Held(repay()) For term + notice-window
Power give-notice Actor lender Recipient guarantor
  Holds when True
  Valid when notice-due() && Not(Violated(notice-due()))
  Creates notified()

// 1.2 and 2. Demand, within the limit, and payment in fifteen days
Var called Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Var unpaid Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Power demand Actor lender Recipient guarantor Related to usd
  Holds when in-default() && notified() && called + usd <= limit && unpaid + usd <= balance
  Valid when in-default() && notified() && called + usd <= limit && unpaid + usd <= balance
  Creates called(called + usd), unpaid(unpaid + usd)
Duty guaranty-due Holder guarantor Claimant lender
  Holds when unpaid > 0
  Due within 15

// 5. The guarantor who pays takes over the claim
Var claim Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Act pay-guaranty Actor guarantor Recipient lender Related to usd
  Holds when usd <= unpaid
  Creates unpaid(unpaid - usd), balance(balance - usd), claim(claim + usd)
Duty reimburse Holder borrower Claimant guarantor
  Holds when claim > 0
Act repay-guarantor Actor borrower Recipient guarantor Related to usd
  Holds when usd <= claim
  Creates claim(claim - usd)

// 4. A change without consent releases the guarantor
Bool consent
Act consent-to-change Actor guarantor Recipient lender
  Holds when True
  Creates consent()
Act change-terms Actor lender Recipient borrower
  Holds when consent()
  Creates released(guarantor) When Not(consent())
  Terminates consent()
Immunity released Holder guarantor Against demand

Clause 1.1 Approved "5151c51fd5ae69f1d34111b51860e1a3e4a761d7dbf53ac17e2629458edad838"
  Definition "Victor Lang, the guarantor, guarantees to Ines Marlow, the lender, the loan of eight thousand dollars that the lender has made to Dana Cole, the borrower."
  Norm " The borrower is in default if the loan is not repaid in full within ninety days after the date of this guaranty." => repay, pay-loan
Clause 1.2 Approved "f6bf507aedd30bb8a2684271afabd5a3251a2787046184717b86f663dfa63e67"
  Norm "While the borrower is in default the lender may demand payment from the guarantor." => demand
  Norm " The guarantor pays what the lender has demanded within fifteen days after the demand." => guaranty-due, pay-guaranty
Clause 2.1 Approved "845c79322d1a3e6ddde0cb41dfa3e50fc09b81da2e53da8ac9b9517e604a4b5d"
  Norm "The guarantor's liability under this guaranty is limited to five thousand dollars in all. The lender may not demand more than remains of that limit, or more than the borrower then owes, and a demand for more has no effect." => demand
Clause 3.1 Approved "d538ca2e2fca21042815be0b2939711a21ae6c98bfea05d41eab4b0429b21040"
  Norm "The lender gives the guarantor notice of the borrower's default within thirty days after the default." => notice-due, give-notice
  Norm " The lender may not demand payment unless that notice was given in time, and a demand made without it has no effect." => demand, give-notice
Clause 4.1 Approved "183acb17eaf24f2be8202efa8c5f4751ecb3ad701cdc9914fdc3dd46ce24cf96"
  Norm "The lender does not change the terms of the loan without the guarantor's consent." => change-terms, consent-to-change
  Norm " If the lender does, the guarantor is released, and no demand made after the change has any effect." => released, change-terms
Clause 5.1 Approved "2826fca41284d59dbedc70aa46ac49d85b47ef736730cda8aa846fcaae60e425"
  Norm "A guarantor who pays the lender takes over the lender's claim against the borrower for the amount paid. The borrower then owes that amount to the guarantor and no longer owes it to the lender." => pay-guaranty, reimburse, repay-guarantor
.
+balance(loan). +called(0). +unpaid(0). +claim(0).
